      "id": "spf:figma",
      "type": [
        "schema:SoftwareApplication",
        "spf:Tool",
        "skos:Concept"
      ],
      "Tool Name": "Figma",
      "Data Type": [
        {
          "id": "spf:tool",
          "label": "Tool"
        }
      ],
      "Tool URL": "https://figma.com",
      "Tool Logo": [
        {
          "name": "figma.png",
          "url": "https://baserow-backend-production20240528124524339000000001.s3.amazonaws.com/user_files/RkZQ8YnIuh2oyvQUZcZDY9XODXPuXrcN_ddfd248ffa9293feb739393a03a821508fada1c701b9b35b1923ff3ee43ed142.png"
        }
      ],
      "Category": "User Experience",
      "Tool Description": "Figma is a design tool where teams build the actual screens of a product, from rough wireframes to polished, clickable prototypes. Because it runs in the browser and lets people work together in real time, it is often where design and development meet, with designers laying out interfaces and handing off clear specs for engineers to build.",
      "Tool Features": "1. Build low fidelity interfaces\n1. Build high fidelity interfaces\n1. Create animations\n1. Create design components\n1. Define the UI styles\n1. Define the specifications for development",
      "Tool Direct Competitors": "1. [Sketch](https://www.sketch.com/)\n1. [InVision](https://www.invisionapp.com/)\n1. [Balsamiq](https://balsamiq.com/)\n1. [Axure](https://www.axure.com/)\n1. [Framer](https://www.framer.com/)",
      "Common Tasks Using the Tool": [
        {
          "id": "spf:wireframing",
